  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>heatmap</keyword>
  <short_description>Create a heatmap chart from a numeric matrix or table.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(C)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(xvalues, yvalues, C)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(tbl, xvar, yvar)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(tbl, xvar, yvar, 'ColorVariable', cvar)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(parent, ...)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>heatmap(..., propertyName, propertyValue)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = heatmap(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>C</param_name>
      <param_description>Numeric matrix used as color data.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>xvalues</param_name>
      <param_description>Labels for matrix columns: cell string, string, character, or numeric vector.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>yvalues</param_name>
      <param_description>Labels for matrix rows: cell string, string, character, or numeric vector.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>tbl</param_name>
      <param_description>Source table used to calculate heatmap values.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>xvar</param_name>
      <param_description>Table variable used for x categories.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>yvar</param_name>
      <param_description>Table variable used for y categories.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>cvar</param_name>
      <param_description>Numeric table variable averaged for each x/y category pair.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>parent</param_name>
      <param_description>Axes or hggroup parent.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>propertyName</param_name>
      <param_description>Supported property name.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>propertyValue</param_name>
      <param_description>Property value.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>h</param_name>
      <param_description>Heatmap chart object containing the heatmap image, grid, labels, and colorbar state.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>heatmap</b> displays a numeric matrix as a scaled color image with row and column labels. For table input, categories are sorted and the color data is aggregated by category pair.</p>
    <p>With <b>heatmap(tbl, xvar, yvar)</b>, color data contains counts and <b>ColorMethod</b> is <b>count</b>. With <b>ColorVariable</b>, color data contains means and <b>ColorMethod</b> is <b>mean</b>.</p>
    <p>This implementation returns a <b>heatmap</b> chart object. The chart <b>UserData</b> contains the fields <b>ChartType</b>, <b>Image</b>, <b>Grid</b>, <b>CellLabels</b>, <b>Colorbar</b>, <b>XData</b>, <b>YData</b>, <b>ColorData</b>, <b>SourceTable</b>, <b>XVariable</b>, <b>YVariable</b>, <b>ColorVariable</b>, <b>ColorMethod</b>, and <b>Options</b>.</p>
    <p>Supported name/value properties are <b>Title</b>, <b>XLabel</b>, <b>YLabel</b>, <b>SourceTable</b>, <b>XVariable</b>, <b>YVariable</b>, <b>ColorVariable</b>, <b>ColorMethod</b>, <b>XData</b>, <b>YData</b>, <b>XDisplayLabels</b>, <b>YDisplayLabels</b>, <b>ColorLimits</b>, <b>Colormap</b>, <b>ColorbarVisible</b>, <b>GridVisible</b>, <b>CellLabelFormat</b>, <b>CellLabelColor</b>, <b>MissingDataLabel</b>, <b>FontColor</b>, <b>FontSize</b>, and <b>Visible</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>Nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Display a numeric heatmap.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[C = [1 2 3; 4 5 6];
heatmap(C);]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img src="../../../../images/heatmap_1.svg" align="middle" generate="true" />
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>Nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Use row and column labels.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[C = [3 7 2; 6 5 8];
heatmap({'A', 'B', 'C'}, {'Low', 'High'}, C, ...
  'Title', 'Scores', 'XLabel', 'Column', 'YLabel', 'Group');]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img src="../../../../images/heatmap_2.svg" align="middle" generate="true" />
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>Nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Create a heatmap from table categories.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[T = table({'B'; 'A'; 'B'}, {'Y'; 'X'; 'X'}, [2; 5; 8], ...
  'VariableNames', {'x', 'y', 'v'});
heatmap(T, 'x', 'y', 'ColorVariable', 'v');]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img src="../../../../images/heatmap_3.svg" align="middle" generate="true" />
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>Nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Customize colors and labels.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data><![CDATA[C = peaks(12);
heatmap(C, 'ColorLimits', [-6 8], 'Colormap', turbo(64), ...
  'CellLabelFormat', '%0.1f', 'GridVisible', 'off');]]></example_item_data>
      <example_item_img src="../../../../images/heatmap_4.svg" align="middle" generate="true" />
    </example_item>
  </examples>
